<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tumed (Altan Khan)</h1><p class="st-meta">1530 CE – 1632 CE (approx.) · capital Guihua (Hohhot)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The realm of Altan Khan in Inner Mongolia, which made peace with Ming China, founded Hohhot and gave the Dalai Lama his title.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altan-khan">Altan Khan</a>, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayan-khan">Dayan Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-yuan">Northern Yuan</a>, became leader of the Tümed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumen">tumen</a> in the 1530s and turned it into the strongest power among the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. His raids reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> capital, which he besieged in 1550, in an effort to force <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> to open border trade.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After a peace in 1571 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altan-khan">Altan Khan</a> the title Shunyi Wang and opened horse markets on the frontier. He welcomed Chinese farmers and craftsmen, many of them refugees, and built the walled town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohhot">Guihua</a> (Hohhot). In 1578 he met the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug</a> lama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonam-gyatso">Sonam Gyatso</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qinghai-lake">Kokonor</a>, gave him the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a> and adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, launching the conversion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altan-khan">Altan Khan's</a> death in 1582 his descendants, guided at first by his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jonggen-khatun">Jönggen Khatun</a>, kept the peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> but lost influence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ligdan-khan">Ligdan Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chahar-mongols">Chahar</a> overran their lands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohhot">Guihua</a> in 1627 to 1628; when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-taiji">Hong Taiji's</a> campaign of 1632 drove him west, the Tümed soon submitted to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-jin-1616-1636">Later Jin</a> (1616-1636).</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1530 CE – 1632 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.15%;width:2.03%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1530 CE – 1632 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guihua (Hohhot)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Altan Khan, Sengge Düküreng</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tibetan Buddhism, Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mongolian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tumed Khanate, Tumed</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1581&amp;focus=tumed-altan-khan" aria-label="Tumed (Altan Khan) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7448 1145 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tumed (Altan Khan) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7768 1401L7817 927M7768 1401L7643 1242M7768 1401L8018 907"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7817 927h0M7643 1242h0M8018 907h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7768 1401h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7768 1401h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guihua. <a href="/atlas?year=1581&amp;focus=tumed-altan-khan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

